              "text": "There are currently **no new episodes** of *The Flash* scheduled to air. \n\nHere is what you need to know regarding the status of the show and the character:\n\n### 1. The CW Series Has Ended\nThe popular CW television series starring Grant Gustin officially concluded its run. The series finale, \"A New World, Part Four\" (Season 9, Episode 13), aired on **May 24, 2023**. After nine seasons and 184 episodes, the story of Barry Allen in the \"Arrowverse\" came to a planned end, and the show was not renewed for a tenth season.\n\n### 2. Beware of Fake Trailers and \"Season 10\" Rumors\nIf you have seen promotional videos, trailers, or articles online claiming that *The Flash* Season 10 is coming or that a reboot movie starring Grant Gustin and Jenna Ortega is releasing, **these are entirely fan-made, concept trailers, or rumors**. There is no official Season 10 or continuation in development.\n\n### 3. Future of the Character in the DCU\nWhile the CW television series is over, DC Studios (under the leadership of James Gunn and Peter Safran) is currently rebooting the entire DC cinematic and television landscape. A new iteration of the Flash will eventually be introduced to this shared universe, but as of now, DC has not announced a release date or a dedicated television show for the next Scarlet Speedster.",
